    <string name="routing_scope_title">What Tono can and cannot recognise</string>
    <string name="routing_scope">Order: 21 cloud video exceptions → 166 AI / named Home entries (plus the Anthropic address range and the Claude, ChatGPT and Grok apps) → explicit cloud list → everything else direct. Matched traffic that fails is paused, never sent direct; matched UDP/QUIC is refused so apps fall back to TCP. Apps using ECH, their own DNS-over-HTTPS, or cached addresses can hide an AI service; that traffic then goes direct. Unrecognised AI is not guaranteed to use Home.</string>
    <string name="routing_platform">On Android all apps, all TCP/UDP ports, IPv4 and IPv6 enter the tunnel. LAN, link-local and multicast stay outside. DNS for direct names uses your network\'s resolver; matched names never reach it. Hotspot clients and apps you exclude below bypass Tono entirely.</string>
